WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.740
- But Joel, you've been working
with "Tiger King," right?

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:04.438
You've been interviewing all the people?

00:00:04.438 --> 00:00:05.673
For Netflix, right?

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:07.563
- Yeah.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:12.890
I'm holding on to the
coattails of that documentary.

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:17.540
They asked me to host the
wrap, the catch-up special

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:19.060
and see where everybody was

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:21.770
that was agreeing to be on camera.

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:25.140
And so, they asked me a
few days before it aired.

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:27.600
And we quickly scrambled together.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:29.290
They had a bunch of people
ready to be interviewed.

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:31.433
So I had barely anything.

00:00:33.044 --> 00:00:36.380
I was just happy to do it,
because I loved the series

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:37.480
and was fascinated by it.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:39.930
And I got to talk to a
lot of the folks involved.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:44.390
After anything I've done in the business

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:45.590
for the last 20 years,

00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:48.471
nothing compared to the response of that.

00:00:48.471 --> 00:00:50.150
(laughs)
I've never been a part

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:53.350
of anything that was that popular, ever.

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:56.440
Combine "The Soup" and
"Community," not even close

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:59.740
to one 40-minute special
- Oh, my God.

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:02.770
- of me going, "How's Oklahoma?"

00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:06.487
So that's basically--
(laughs)

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:11.190
- Well Octavia, what have
you been binge-watching?

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:13.640
- I've been watching "Little Fires."

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:14.560
- I haven't seen that!

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:16.305
I wanna see that, is that so good?

00:01:16.305 --> 00:01:18.473
- Oh, so good, so good.

00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:22.600
I'm not kidding you, I'm
going back to simpler times.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:25.410
I'm watchin' "The Waltons."

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:26.243
- Wow.
- I love it.

00:01:26.243 --> 00:01:28.070
- And "Little House on the Prairie,"

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:30.763
things before times of Corona.

00:01:32.311 --> 00:01:34.200
- You're in a dark place if
you're needing that kind.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.073
You're like, all of a sudden--

00:01:35.073 --> 00:01:36.017
- I need it, I need it.

00:01:36.017 --> 00:01:36.850
I need Pa.

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:38.488
Ma, Pa, Half Pint.
- You're goin' way back.

00:01:38.488 --> 00:01:39.321
- I need it.

00:01:39.321 --> 00:01:40.597
- You're like, "I need nostalgia

00:01:40.597 --> 00:01:42.940
"from whenever I could go
ride my bike and be outside."

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:46.340
- I like how, "I'm going
back before Corona."

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:48.090
I was like, "You could've done ER."

00:01:49.143 --> 00:01:51.540
(laughs)
I mean, that was 25 years ago.

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:52.820
But you decided to go back
- ER?

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:54.896
- almost 40 years ago.

00:01:54.896 --> 00:01:55.729
50 years ago.
- Way more.

